      "body": "## Motivation\n\nHost-resident INT8 embeddings can retain quantization scales on CUDA while their weights and lookup indices are on CPU, causing device mismatches during embedding lookup.\n\n## Modifications\n\n* Move the restored embedding module to CPU before installing host-gather hooks, keeping its weights, scales, and buffers together.\n* Add CUDA regressions for rowwise and scalar INT8 embeddings.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nRecorded validation: 14 focused tests passed.\n\nThe new regressions verify CPU weights and scales, CUDA outputs, and exact equality with the original embedding lookup.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot run.\n\n## Checklist\n\n* [x] Format your code according to the pre-commit guidance.\n* [x] Add unit tests.\n* [ ] Update documentation.\n* [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results.\n* [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38524341352](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38524341352)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38524341319](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38524341319)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38524341252](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38524341252)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
